# Responsive design by audience

Tailwind uses mobile-first **breakpoints** (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`). Product layout strategy is **not**
one-size-fits-all — match the primary device for each audience.

## Strategy map

- **Public site** `(public)/**` — phone, **mobile-first** (design and test at ~375px first)
- **Member app** `(member)/**` — phone, **mobile-first**
- **Staff ops** `(admin)/admin/**` except owner settings — phone/tablet on floor, **mobile-first**
- **Trainer flows** `(member)/trainer/**` — phone, **mobile-first**
- **Owner CMS** `(admin)/admin/settings/**`, `src/components/admin/settings/**` — desktop,
  **desktop-first** (usable on mobile, not optimized for it)

When unsure, use route group + role: day-to-day gym use → mobile-first; site builder / brand / config →
desktop-first.

## Mobile-first surfaces (required)

- Layout and typography readable at 320–375px without horizontal scroll
- Tap targets ≥ 44px; primary actions easy to reach (avoid hover-only critical paths)
- Stack columns by default; add columns at `sm:` / `md:` only when space allows
- Forms: full-width inputs, clear labels, sticky or obvious submit on long flows (e.g. PR submit)
- Test member/staff flows as if used one-handed on the gym floor

## Desktop-first owner CMS (required)

- Two-column editor + preview is the default — use `SettingsEditorShell`, `PreviewDeviceFrame`
- Dense tables, side nav, and wide `max-w-7xl` layouts are OK on desktop
- On mobile: stack editor above preview, no clipped overflow, scrollable panels, save still reachable
- Preview-first on small screens with jump-to-edit is fine (`lg:hidden` edit buttons) — match existing
  settings patterns
- Do not sacrifice desktop productivity to force mobile parity on configuration screens

## Shared

- Dark gym aesthetic via theme CSS vars — see `project-foundation.mdc`
- Reuse `Button`, `Card`, `Input` from `src/components/ui/`
- Owner-facing copy and field help — see `owner-friendly-ui.mdc`
